<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $2.7 bln in June 9 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $2.7 bln in June 9 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $2.7 billion in the June 9 week to $3,907.0 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $2.8 billion to $5,065.5 billion. M-1 was off $11.7 billion to $1,058.9 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,906.8 billion versus $3,903.2 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
